// Morrowind groundcover: species, rule table and the land textures that feed each rule channel (slice GC-2b2;
// spec `bevyrrowind/docs/specs/groundcover-adapter.md` "First species set"; core types `sf_groundcover`).
// Read by `mw_world::groundcover`. Units: metres, degrees, instances per m². Every density, footprint, range,
// slope and weight is a `Guess`, to be set by the owner's look loop on the test scenes, not copied from a mod.
//
// Model keys are VFS paths in the form `mw_world::model_path` gives a STAT's model ("meshes/f/....nif").
// Rule weights: a species' weight at a point is Σ (rule weight × channel weight); its expected instances per m²
// are that weight × `density`. Within one channel the weights are shares, summing to about 1 for a full meadow.
